    "EasingFunction": {
      "description": "Easing functions are used to interpolate between two values over time.\n\nCustom easing functions can be implemented with cubic Bézier. The control points are defined with `points` field by providing four numerical values: `x1`, `y1`, `x2` and `y2`. The `x1` and `x2` values have to be in the range `[0; 1]`. The cubic Bézier result is clamped to the range `[0; 1]`. You can find example control point configurations at https://easings.net/.",
